WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.625
What about that max-epoch parameter, N?

00:00:02.705 --> 00:00:04.428
Ablating N over one, five,

00:00:04.508 --> 00:00:09.214
and ten on Large models gives TyDi QA scores of
eighty-two point two,

00:00:09.294 --> 00:00:12.682
eighty-one point five, and eighty-one point eight.

00:00:12.762 --> 00:00:16.774
Disallowing repeats entirely, N equals one, comes
out best,

00:00:16.854 --> 00:00:18.646
though the effect is small.

00:00:18.726 --> 00:00:23.363
At a four-times-larger budget, UniMax scores
eighty-three point one,

00:00:23.443 --> 00:00:29.605
versus eighty-two point eight for temperature and
eighty-one point two for tau equals one.

00:00:29.685 --> 00:00:35.847
The loss curves tell the story: high-temperature
overfitting grows more severe with scale,

00:00:35.927 --> 00:00:37.650
while UniMax stays stable.
